# Code-review + graphify

## When

`code-review` / `review` / `/code-review`, or review of branch / PR / uncommitted / “review since X”.

## Rules

1. List touched files/symbols (`git diff --name-only` / status).
2. Graphify first: `query` / `path` / `explain` on those symbols — pass **subgraph** to Standards/Spec subagents (not whole tree / full `GRAPH_REPORT.md`).
3. Put the graphify obligation in every review subagent prompt.
4. Prefer boundary findings (cross-imports, unexpected paths, untouched neighbors).
5. Missing `graph.json`: say so; continue with diff. Stale graph: note it; rebuild only if needed and not Ask mode.
6. Diff remains source of what changed; graphify orients.

## Done

Report which graphify queries/paths ran; subagents got scoped graph context.

## Pitfalls

Standards/Spec without graphify; pasting full `GRAPH_REPORT.md`; skipping `path` on cross-domain coupling.
